
========================================================================
  THE THREE GRAPHS AT n=5: SETUP
========================================================================

  n=5:
  Tile positions (non-base arcs): m = C(4,2) = 6
  Arc positions (all arcs):       M = C(5,2) = 10
  Base path arcs:                 4 = M - m = 4

  GRAPH 1 (WIGGLY): Q_6 with 2^6 = 64 vertices
  GRAPH 2 (WAGGLY): complement of Q_6
  GRAPH 3 (ARC-FLIP): Q_10 with 2^10 = 1024 vertices

  All pairs:  [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
  Base pairs: [(0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4)]
  Tile pairs: [(0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 4)]

========================================================================
  GRAPH 1: THE TILING HYPERCUBE (WIGGLY)
========================================================================

  Tiling hypercube: 64 tilings → 12 iso classes

========================================================================
  GRAPH 3: THE FULL ARC-FLIP HYPERCUBE
========================================================================

  Arc hypercube: 1024 tournaments → 12 iso classes
  Arc classes: 12 unmerged → 10 merged

========================================================================
  THE TILING SUBFACE INSIDE THE ARC HYPERCUBE
========================================================================

  Arc pair ordering: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
  Base arc bit positions: [0, 4, 7, 9] (always 0 for tilings)
  Tile arc bit positions: [1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 8] (free bits)

  Tiling subface: 64 points in the 6-dim face of Q_10
  (Base path bits all = 0)

========================================================================
  BLUE/BLACK: WHERE DO THEY LIVE?
========================================================================

  BLUE/BLACK LINES ARE NOT IN THE TILING HYPERCUBE Q_6.
  They connect tilings in DIFFERENT base-path frames.

  For a tiling t of tournament T with base path P₀:
  Blue/black goes to tilings of T^op with DIFFERENT base paths.
  These other base paths are HPs of T^op, relabeled to P₀.

  So blue/black jumps OUTSIDE the hypercube Q_6
  into the larger arc-hypercube Q_10.

  EXAMPLE: tracing blue/black from the transitive tiling

  Transitive tiling: t=000000 (arc bits: 0000000000)
  T^op in arc space: 1111111111
  T^op base-path bits: [1, 1, 1, 1] (all 1 = reversed)

  T^op has 1 Hamiltonian paths
  Blue/black targets from transitive: 1 tilings
  Target classes: {11: 1}

